<article class="env-proposition" id="27B68F">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/27B68F">Proposition <span data-tag="27B68F">5.0.0.1</span>.</a> Let $F: \calA \rightarrow \Set $ be a contravariant functor from $\calA $ to the category of sets. Then $F$ is representable by an object of $\calA $ if and only if it carries colimits in $\calA $ to limits in $\Set $. </p>
